To set the BGP Local Preference to 150 within a policy statement term 'TERM1', you would typically use the following configuration in a router's BGP policy. Assuming you are using a Juniper device, the configuration would look like this:

```
policy-options {
    policy-statement TERM1 {
        term set-local-preference {
            from {
                // Specify the conditions for the routes you want to match
            }
            then {
                local-preference 150;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

The `local-preference` attribute influences inbound traffic engineering by guiding BGP speakers to prefer paths with higher local preference values.  The `from` block within the `term` allows you to define matching criteria for the routes to which this preference will be applied.  If no `from` clause is present, the `local-preference` will be applied to all routes.
